-- Candidate 5 — CRITICAL, row_type incident. Dispatch E5.
-- Four quantities the chapter authored (theta, alpha, tau, W) were dropped by a
-- closed six-row table with a bare "continue" — no row, no throw, no console
-- message, no gate failure, and no Zod enum to fail against. FIXED in this
-- dispatch, together with the three other silent-skip surfaces on the same
-- scenario and the loud-warning channel that makes the whole class visible.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
INSERT INTO engine_bug_queue (
    bug_class, title, severity, owner_cluster, root_cause, prevention_rule,
    probe_type, probe_logic, status, concepts_affected, fixed_in_files,
    discovered_in_session, row_type
) VALUES (
    'rbr_authored_token_silently_skipped_when_the_engine_lacks_the_row',
    'Four taught quantities authored into rigid_body_rotation readouts (theta, alpha, tau, W) rendered NOTHING and warned NOTHING — a closed HUD table dropped every unrecognised token with a bare continue, and field_3d_config is modelled in Zod at no depth, so there was not even an enum for the token to fail against',
    'CRITICAL',
    'peter_parker:field3d_surgeon',
    'RBR_RO_META was a closed six-row table (I, omega, L, KE, dLdt, F_pull) and BOTH readers — rbrRebuildReadout at build and rbrWriteReadouts every frame — filtered it with "var meta = RBR_RO_META[k]; if (!meta) continue;". An authored readouts[] token with no row therefore produced no row, no disabled row, no throw, no console message and no gate failure. This is strictly worse than a missing enum member: field_3d_config is not modelled in Zod at ANY depth, so readouts ["theta","alpha"] validated, seeded into simulation_cache, rendered, and passed THE EYE — the turntable really does spin, so every pixel gate is green — and could reach a founder seal with the TAUGHT QUANTITY simply absent from the screen. Only a human reading the sim against the physics block catches it. The same silent filter ran on three further surfaces of the same scenario: reference_marks[].surface (a mark naming a quantity with no meta row is never drawn and never matches, and the surface union in the TypeScript interface was NARROWER than the runtime table, which is the same divergence from the other side), reference_marks form ''tick'' (only ever drawn on the KE bar, so a tick on any other surface, or a tick in a state with no ke_bar.max_j, vanished), and controls_visible (already fixed for newtons_laws_body by dispatch E3 under bug_class nlb_seam_r_slider_tokens_declared_but_unwired — the rbr copy of the same filter was still silent). MEASURED BLAST RADIUS: three concepts blocked. rotational_kinematics and tau_eq_i_alpha (Desk D) cannot print theta or alpha at all and did no wave-1 authoring because of it; rotational_work_energy (Desk A) cannot print W = tau.theta. Rule 31 additionally makes a legal explore state impossible for both Desk-D concepts, because there was no applied-torque control of any kind — the taught variable of tau_eq_i_alpha had no dial. The class is not scenario-local: Desk A closing analysis counted SIX separate defects across this chapter with one shape — something authored, accepted by every gate, that does nothing, silently — and judged that one console.warn per class would have caught five of the six at authoring time. A-18 (dead formula assemblies, fixed by E1) survived a complete authoring cycle — architect, physics-author, json-author, quality-auditor, eye-walker, founder-proxy Checkpoint B — at a clean 35/35.',
    'A LOOKUP THAT FILTERS UNKNOWN KEYS MUST SAY SO, ONCE, OUT LOUD. Every "if (!table[token]) continue;" over an AUTHORED token is a silent-drop site and must warn (never throw — the createTubeLine scar says an authoring typo must not take the scene down); warn once per distinct token per state so it cannot become per-frame spam. The defect is invisible for exactly as long as it is silent, and no downstream gate can see it: a Zod schema that does not model the block cannot reject the token, and a pixel gate passes because the rest of the scene is correct. Corollaries, each of which cost a separate decision here: (a) A CLOSED SET IN THE TYPE SYSTEM MUST EQUAL THE CLOSED SET AT RUNTIME — a surface union narrower than the runtime table reintroduces the same defect from the type side, so widen every parallel enum in the SAME commit; (b) A DERIVED QUANTITY IS PRINTED FROM THE RESOLVED STATE, NEVER FROM THE AUTHORED SCHEDULE — the applied-torque row must show the torque the integrator is actually running at, because at a rest clamp the authored value prints tau = -1.53 beside alpha = 0.00 and I = 3.06, contradicting tau = I.alpha in a frozen frame in the very concept whose atomic claim it is; (c) A RATE IS THE FINITE DIFFERENCE OF THE QUANTITY THE ENGINE ACTUALLY INTEGRATES, not the analytic form — alpha as (omega(t) - omega(t-h))/h stays true at a rest clamp, under a live dI/dt (it carries the -(omega/I).dI/dt term the analytic tau/I drops) and at every engage edge, and it keeps torque out of a kinematics concept taught before torque exists (Rule 25); its lookback must be CLAMPED TO THE RUN ANCHOR or the first frame after a re-pin differences across the re-seed and prints a spike that reads as an uncaused torque; (d) A NEW CUMULATIVE QUANTITY RIDES AN EXISTING CACHED INTEGRATOR, NEVER A NEW ACCUMULATOR — work is the integral of tau.dtheta and dtheta is theta own grid step, so W composes over the SAME walk with the SAME rewind rule and inherits the pin/rewind contract for free; it is the SIGNED integral (a brake does negative work; a drive carrying the body through zero does negative work then positive), so |tau|.|theta| would be monotonic and wrong in exactly the states the concept exists to teach; (e) A UNIT CHOICE THAT SPANS A CHAPTER LIVES IN ONE CONSTANT AND IS NEVER A PER-CONCEPT OVERRIDE — six turntable concepts disagreeing on whether theta is radians or degrees is what APPARATUS_CONTRACT.md section 3 forbids, and tau = I.alpha only holds in radians, so a degrees theta beside a rad/s^2 alpha is incoherent on one HUD; (f) THE CONCEPT PRINTING A NEGATIVE IS RARELY THE ONE CARRYING THE UNICODE DISCIPLINE — rotational_kinematics prints alpha = -0.50, so the minus must be U+2212 from the shared formatter (Rule 34c), which is only true if every new value path goes through that formatter and not through toFixed.',
    'js_eval',
    'Brace-match the rbr readout + control + physics surface out of FIELD_3D_RENDERER_CODE for BOTH the pre-change and post-change files (the check_bonding_scene extraction idiom) and run it against a stub window/document, so the REAL config parsing, the REAL innerHTML build and the REAL per-frame writes are exercised rather than a reimplementation. Every delta assertion is paired with an ABSOLUTE FLOOR. ASSERT (1) BYTE-IDENTICAL A/B: a state authoring NONE of the new tokens produces character-identical readout innerHTML and KE-bar innerHTML, an identical controls_visible token list, and across a 751-frame sweep (0..12000 ms at 16 ms, spanning a restart and its blank window) every row textContent and style.display, the KE-bar fill width, the restart badge display and Object.is-equal theta / L / KE — 0 differences — and the new build emits ZERO warnings on that state. (2) EACH NEW ROW RENDERS with the right id, the right Unicode glyph (theta, alpha, tau, W) and the right unit (rad, rad/s^2, N.m, J) at dp 2, with absolute floors: I = 3.74 exactly, tau = 1.20, alpha = tau/I = 0.3209, theta = the closed form 0.6417 MINUS exactly the pre-existing forward-Euler grid lag (1/2).alpha.h.t, W = 0.7639. (3) tau IS THE RESOLVED TORQUE: at a rest clamp (drive -1.53 against brake 2.0, I = 3.06) the HUD prints tau = 0.00 beside alpha = 0.00 and I = 3.06 — NOT the authored -1.53 — and a negative control with the brake at 0.53 prints the breakaway -1.00 whose leading character is U+2212, not ASCII 0x2D, with alpha = -0.33 = tau/I. (4) alpha EQUALS the 16 ms finite difference of omega EXACTLY (max |diff| = 0 over 1016..5000 ms), blanks to the em-dash inside a re-pin window exactly as the pre-existing rows do, and does NOT spike on the first frame after the blank ends. (5) W SURVIVES PIN/REWIND: theta and W at 3000 ms are bit-identical across a 3000 -> 9000 -> 3000 -> 500 -> 9000 -> 3000 chain, and W(9000) is bit-identical after a rewind; W == tau x theta bit-exactly for a constant tau (the composition contract), == KE(t) - KE(0) to within the same Euler lag (0.8% here) both for a monotonic spin-up and through a real omega sign change, goes NEGATIVE while the drive opposes the spin and rises again once it drives the other way, and is provably NOT |tau|.|theta|. (6) WARNINGS: an unknown readouts token authored TWICE warns exactly once; an unknown reference_marks surface, a tick on a non-KE surface, a tick with no ke_bar.max_j and an unknown controls_visible token each warn exactly once; all warns carry one prefix and name the state; 125 further frames add zero warns; the SAME bad token in a second state warns again. (7) the applied-torque control builds a discoverable _row id with a SIGNED range, keeps the canonical row order, and a live write spins a rest-seeded body up to exactly tau/I = 0.2139 rad/s at 1 s and reverses on a negative write. LIMITS, stated because they matter: this reads the EMITTED SOURCE against a stub DOM, so it proves arithmetic, parsing and rendered STRINGS and proves NOTHING about pixels, layout, collision, camera framing, occlusion or a real trusted drag; it cannot see a stray backtick terminating the template literal (npm run check:renderer-syntax caught exactly that during this dispatch, in a comment); and the desk canaries (newton_second_law, coulombs_law) do not exercise rbr at all, so they prove only no collateral damage OUTSIDE rbr. It is a smoke test. The gate is Desk A verifying this on a real concept with its own seed key after it lands on master.',
    'FIXED',
    ARRAY['rotational_kinematics', 'tau_eq_i_alpha', 'rotational_work_energy']::text[],
    ARRAY['src/lib/renderers/field_3d_renderer.ts']::text[],
    'rotmech Phase 0c-3 — Desk E dispatch E5 2026-08-05',
    'incident'
