-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- Candidate 6 — AMENDMENT, NOT A NEW ROW. Dispatch E7.
--
-- bug_class is the upsert key and this defect is a RECURRENCE of an existing
-- row, so this is an UPDATE of
--   field3d_arrowhelper_shaft_invisible_when_collinear_with_apparatus_line
-- and NOT an insert. Applying it as an INSERT would mint a duplicate of a scar
-- the fleet has already paid for twice (lom-g force_rig, and now rotmech rbr).
--
-- owner_cluster is DELIBERATELY LEFT AT the historical 'peter_parker:renderer_
-- primitives' string. That tag maps to pcpl-surgeon today, but the fleet rule
-- is never to migrate a historical tag string; the CURRENT owner of this
-- surface (peter_parker:field3d_surgeon) is recorded in the text instead. Do
-- not "fix" the tag.
--
-- The recurrence: rigid_body_rotation shipped TWO ArrowHelpers whose shafts
-- run collinear with an opaque apparatus cylinder — the L vector inside the
-- axle, the pull force along the rod. The lom-g row's prevention rule was
-- followed only in its (a) half (a z-offset), which is why it recurred; the
-- rule is rewritten below so that the z-offset clause is explicitly NOT a fix
-- and the radius/emissive ratio is a WRITTEN CONSTANT rather than an eyeball.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
UPDATE engine_bug_queue SET
    title = 'A vector drawn along the apparatus line it describes is swallowed by it: ArrowHelper''s shaft is a zero-width THREE.Line. RECURRED on rigid_body_rotation (rotmech 0c-3) in both of that scenario''s vectors — the L arrow inside the axle and the pull arrow along the rod — one release after the force_rig fix',
    severity = 'MAJOR',
    root_cause = 'THREE.ArrowHelper draws its shaft as a THREE.Line, and WebGL ignores linewidth on essentially every desktop driver, so the shaft is permanently 1px no matter what the code asks for. An arrow in its own perpendicular lane survives this; an arrow COLLINEAR with an opaque apparatus cylinder does not — it lives inside the very object it measures. FIRST OCCURRENCE (lom-g force_rig): a string tension acting along its own 0.022-radius string rendered as a bare floating head. RECURRENCE (rotmech rigid_body_rotation, dispatch E7): BOTH of the scenario''s vectors. (1) The L vector sat on the axle centreline at (0, 0.22, 0) inside an opaque CylinderGeometry(0.07, 0.07, 3.4) — measured on the frozen frames, 15 px of ink in S1 in an 11x6 bbox, a 5.7x change in |L| moving a 7-pixel smear, the material colour #42A5F5 never appearing anywhere on screen, and in the spin-flipped state the arrow ENTIRELY ABSENT with the axle unbroken and not even the cone head visible. The axle radius 0.07 was larger than the arrow''s own CONE radius 0.08 by so little that the head was swallowed too, which is why nothing at all showed. (2) The pull force is RADIAL, i.e. collinear with the rod (CylinderGeometry 0.05), and at the beat that matters — F = m.omega^2.r = 3.60 N with the masses still out at r = 0.80 — it is 0.252 world units, almost exactly the rod''s own tip overhang, drawn in a near-identical pale tone against that overhang. F = m.omega^2.r with omega proportional to 1/I INVERTS the visibility: the arrow is SMALLEST exactly on the cause beat it exists to explain and largest after the slide is over, so an explore-range spot check reads as fine. TWO PRIOR DIAGNOSES ON THIS SURFACE WERE WRONG and cost real dispatch time: it was read as a scaling bug (it is not — the 0.20 world-per-kg.m^2/s scale runs correctly, 0.918 units at L = 4.59 against 0.458 at 2.29) and then as a length-floor bug (it is not — 0.070 x 3.60 = 0.252 clears the 0.16 floor with 1.58x margin). Neither is the defect; occlusion is. THREE RIDE-ALONGS ON THE SAME PRIMITIVE, all found while fixing it: (a) the L map''s minimum RBR_L_ARROW_MIN = 0.22 drew a visible arrow at L = 0 — a rendered lie standing beside a readout printing L = 0.00 — while its maximum 1.80 CLIPPED every |L| above 9.00, so length stopped meaning magnitude exactly where the explore sliders live; (b) the sign-colour channel was dead — RBR_NEG_COLOR had exactly ONE consumer, lArrow.setColor, which recoloured a shaft nothing could see, and the paired rbr_l_label was built in the positive colour with an update that wrote only .position, so the amber/blue pair a teacher is meant to read the sign from never appeared on screen at all; (c) an ArrowHelper''s MeshBasicMaterial/LineBasicMaterial have NO .emissive, so applyGlowEmphasis''s focal brighten on rbr_l_arrow (fired from three authored sites in angular_momentum.json) was a silent no-op — a glow focal that changed nothing.',
    prevention_rule = 'A VECTOR COLLINEAR WITH APPARATUS NEEDS A REAL MESH SHAFT AND A DECLARED SEPARABILITY RATIO — and the ratio must be a WRITTEN CONSTANT, not an eyeball. (a) The shaft is a CylinderGeometry mesh parented into the arrow group, never a THREE.Line and therefore never a THREE.ArrowHelper. (b) The apparatus line is made THINNER AND DIMMER THAN THE SHAFT BY CONSTRUCTION, with the ratio named in the constants next to both radii — this is TWO-SIDED and the apparatus geometry is IN SCOPE: in the recurrence the axle was not merely thicker than the shaft, it was thicker than the arrow''s cone, so no amount of arrow work alone could have fixed it. (c) DIMMER MEANS MEASURED, NOT NOMINAL: the recurrence''s axle (#90A4AE) and its L arrow (#42A5F5) had WCAG relative luminances within 2% of each other — a 1.02:1 contrast ratio, i.e. no tonal separation at all — and the arrow''s green and blue channels CLIP under a bright emissive, so the only remaining lever is darkening the apparatus. Measure the rendered stroke luminances on a real frame and drive the apparatus base tone down until the ratio clears 3:1; a palette-name choice is not evidence. (d) A Z-OFFSET IS NOT A FIX FOR THIS CLASS. It hides the defect at the camera angle it was eyeballed at and restores it at the next, and on a SPINNING scenario it inverts depth every half turn; the first occurrence''s fix used one and the class recurred anyway. Prefer real geometry; depthTest:false is likewise not a substitute (and is actively wrong on a rotating apparatus). (e) ASSERT DRAWN GEOMETRY, NOT A LUMINANCE DELTA. A probe that asserts "a measurable increase when focal" PASSES on a build where the vector is still invisible — fifteen occluded pixels getting brighter satisfies it. A delta cannot detect an ABSENCE. Assert instead that the shaft mesh EXISTS, that its geometry type is a cylinder and not a line, that its radius exceeds the apparatus radius by the constant-declared ratio, and that its drawn tip-to-tail length tracks the magnitude — then pair every delta with an ABSOLUTE FLOOR. (f) A MAGNITUDE-TO-LENGTH MAP IS BOUNDED AND ASYMPTOTIC, NEVER FLOORED-AND-CLIPPED: true zero below an epsilon so a zero quantity draws NOTHING, exactly linear through a knee placed ABOVE the whole reachable band so the taught band is proportional with a zero intercept, and asymptotic above the knee with a continuous first derivative so the explore corners degrade instead of freezing. (g) TWO QUANTITIES DO NOT SHARE ONE MAP — newtons and kg.m^2/s are not commensurable; separability from the apparatus is shared, the scale is not. (h) A COLOUR CHANNEL WITH ONE CONSUMER IS AN UNTESTED CHANNEL: if a sign or state is encoded in colour, EVERY surface that names the quantity (the vector AND its label AND its readout) carries the same colour from the same expression, or the encoding is invisible in exactly the frames it exists for. (i) A FOCAL BRIGHTEN NEEDS A MATERIAL THAT CAN BRIGHTEN — a glow pass that writes emissiveIntensity is a silent no-op on any material without .emissive, so a vector built for emphasis is built on MeshPhongMaterial or the emphasis never happens.',
    probe_type = 'js_eval',
    probe_logic = 'Drive the REAL emitted renderer in a headless browser (assembleField3DHtml is a pure function, so no cache seed and no DB are needed) and DIFFERENCE an arrow-ON frame against a byte-identical arrow-OFF twin state, so the measured ink is the vector''s and nothing else''s. GEOMETRY FIRST, because a delta probe cannot detect an absence: capture the scene at construction, walk it for the vector''s id, and assert the group''s FIRST child geometry.type is CylinderGeometry (not Line/BufferGeometry), its radiusTop equals the declared shaft radius, the apparatus mesh''s radiusTop equals the declared apparatus radius, and shaftR/apparatusR equals the declared ratio EXACTLY. Then assert drawn tip-to-tail length (shaft scale.y + head scale.y) is exactly linear in the magnitude with a zero intercept across the reachable band, that it is exactly 0 at magnitude 0 AND that both child meshes are then .visible === false. PIXEL FLOORS, all ABSOLUTE, none a delta: (1) the vector''s ink in the diff clears a px floor at the guided magnitude; (2) STROKE CONTRAST measured as the median luminance of the vector''s own ink against the median luminance of the APPARATUS PIXELS THE VECTOR COVERS in the OFF twin (an average over the whole footprint is mostly background and flatters the number by 2x — do not use it); (3) a sign/direction flip changes at least N px inside the apparatus column; (4) two frames of the SAME pinned state are byte-identical, which proves the rewind contract for the vector at the same time. LIMITS, stated because they matter: the projected PIXEL length of a vector is NOT exactly linear in the magnitude under a perspective camera even when the drawn world length is — foreshortening varies along the axis, so a pixel-ratio floor of the form len(a)/len(b) = a/b will read several percent high (measured 6.13 against a true 5.71 on a vector pointing at the camera''s up axis) and a bbox measurement is worse still because a cone projects width as well as length. Assert the WORLD drawn length for linearity and treat the pixel ratio as monotonicity evidence only. This probe also proves nothing about camera framing, cue ordering, trusted drags, or a real concept''s authored states; it is a smoke test, and the gate is a real EYE run on a concept that uses the scenario.',
    status = 'FIXED',
    concepts_affected = ARRAY['equilibrium_of_particles', 'uniform_circular_motion', 'angular_momentum', 'rotational_work_energy', 'conservation_of_angular_momentum']::text[],
    fixed_in_files = ARRAY['src/lib/renderers/field_3d_renderer.ts']::text[],
    discovered_in_session = 'lom-g Phase 0 force_rig bring-up 2026-07-30; RECURRED and re-fixed rotmech Phase 0c-3 — Desk E dispatch E7 2026-08-06',
    row_type = 'incident'
WHERE bug_class = 'field3d_arrowhelper_shaft_invisible_when_collinear_with_apparatus_line';


-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- Candidate 7 — CRITICAL, row_type directive.
-- THE METHODOLOGY ROW. Bigger than any single dispatch: it is the primary
-- evidence standard used by every dispatch in PR #29, and it cannot distinguish
-- a healthy baseline from a dead one.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
INSERT INTO engine_bug_queue (
    bug_class, title, severity, owner_cluster, root_cause, prevention_rule,
    probe_type, probe_logic, status, concepts_affected, fixed_in_files,
    discovered_in_session, row_type
) VALUES (
    'byte_identical_ab_against_a_dead_baseline_reads_as_proof_of_correctness',
    'A byte-identical A/B proves non-regression against previous behaviour, never correctness -- when the baseline is dead, "0 differing" is the EXPECTED output of a broken state and the method cannot tell it from a healthy one',
    'CRITICAL',
    'peter_parker:field3d_surgeon',
    'The standard back-compat evidence for an engine dispatch is an A/B: extract the pre-change and post-change emitted code, drive both over a matrix of states and instants, and assert the outputs are identical wherever the change is not meant to apply. That is a sound test of NON-REGRESSION and it is silently unsound as a test of HEALTH, because a state that was already broken produces identical output on both legs. The two readings are indistinguishable in the result: "17/17 identical" is what a healthy untouched state looks like AND what a corpse looks like. Concretely, dispatch E2 (nlb_rolling_branch_has_no_kinematic_gate, commit 1a889bc) reported "rolling_on_incline 17/17 identical" as proof its blast radius was nil, and shipped. Desk B then established by RUNTIME -- MD5 over dumped frames -- that rolling_on_incline is entirely non-functional: STATE_8, the Rule-37 sandbox guaranteed to run continuously, is ONE hash across t=0, t=5000, t=10000 and the frozen pin. Those 17 states were identical because they were dead before AND after. The A/B could not have caught it: it drove the branch-selection logic and never asked whether b.v advanced. The same shape applies to every headline number in that PR -- E3''s "11 concepts, 58 states, 94 bodies, 0 differing" and E4''s "125,280 L samples all Object.is-equal" are equally real and equally silent about whether the states they cover were alive. This is the same family as the gate defects the chapter has now hit repeatedly (an unknown readout token skipped in silence; THE EYE''s three dense-motion gates all passing on a totally static scene): a check that cannot fail is being read as a check that passed.',
    'EVERY A/B MUST ASSERT LIVENESS ON THE QUANTITY UNDER TEST BEFORE THE COMPARISON MEANS ANYTHING. Concretely, three additions, and the first is load-bearing. (a) LIVENESS PRECONDITION: before comparing legs, assert on the PRE-CHANGE leg that the quantity the dispatch is about actually changes over the window -- if b.v is the subject, assert b.v takes more than one distinct value across the frames being compared. If it does not, the baseline is dead and "identical" carries no information; say so in the report instead of quoting it as evidence. (b) NEGATIVE CONTROL, the shape Desk B used and the reason it caught this: include in the same run a case that MUST differ, and show that it does. Desk B''s STATE_7 param_ramp produced a different hash at every timestamp while STATE_8 produced one, which is what made "one hash" a finding rather than a suspicion. An A/B with no negative control cannot distinguish "nothing changed" from "nothing is running". (c) NAME THE CLAIM PRECISELY IN THE REPORT: an A/B licenses "this change did not alter behaviour X", never "behaviour X is correct". A dispatch whose acceptance depends on correctness needs a RUNTIME observation -- frames, hashes, or a verifier desk on a real concept -- and an emitted-code probe is a smoke test, never the gate. Add the liveness assertion to the standing verify chain alongside renderer-syntax / tsc / validate.',
    'js_eval',
    'Reproduce the failure of the method, then the fix. FAILURE LEG: take any A/B harness that reports "N states identical" for a scenario, and for each covered state also record whether the quantity under test took more than one distinct value across the compared window on the PRE-change leg. Assert that at least one covered state reports a single distinct value -- i.e. the corpus being compared contains dead states that the identity result did not distinguish. On rolling_on_incline before E11 this is all 8 states. FIX LEG: assert the harness now refuses to report identity as evidence for any state that failed the liveness precondition, and that a negative control state (one that must differ) is present and does differ in the same run. End-to-end cross-check: md5sum over the dense PNG series of the state in question -- one hash across the series is proof of death regardless of what any A/B reports.',
    'OPEN',
    ARRAY['rolling_on_incline', 'pure_rolling']::text[],
